If possible, try not to use `useBreakpoint` or `useMobile`.

### Organism/PricingTable/PricingTableSectionHeader.vue

Renders a `<tr>` + `<th>`

For props, see `PricingTableSection` (except `rows`)

### Organism/PricingTable/PricingTableRowHeader.vue

Renders a `<th>`

| Prop | Default | Type |
| --- | --- | --- |
| title | - | `string` |
| titleHref | - | `string | undefined`  
If set, the whole cell is a link |
| description | - | `string`  
Rendered below title |
| subFeatures | - | `string[] | undefined`  
Each given string is rendered as a single text line to indicate sub-features |
| hasDifference | - | `boolean`  
Indicates that all values are the same for all plans. Used for comparing differences between plans. |

### Organism/PricingTable/PricingTableRowValue.vue

Renders a `<td>`

| Prop | Default | Type |
| --- | --- | --- |
| title | - | `string | undefined` |
| description | - | `string | undefined` |
| isHighlight | - | `boolean | undefined `  
Renders the title as rainbow text |
| linkText | - | `string | undefined` |
| linkHref | - | `string | undefined` |
| subFeatures | - | `boolean[] | undefined `  
Each boolean renders a feature-icon. true indicates that the feature is included, false indicates that it is not. |

Order of rendered elements is:

1. subFeatures checkmarks / minus-signs
2. title
3. description
4. linkText

Note that if the only given prop is subFeatures with more than one item, we need to add padding to the top to align with the RowHeader, see:

